     "explanation": "Roughly 30% (with 20% as a safer target for freelancers with few active clients) is a commonly cited concentration threshold, borrowed from portfolio-risk thinking in personal finance—beyond that point, the loss of a single client creates a disproportionate, destabilizing hit to total income. Below 5% would be excessively conservative for most solo freelancers with limited client capacity, and claiming concentration doesn't matter ignores one of the best-documented risks in independent work.",
